# Fires the work-anniversary bot each morning, then twice more as a safety net.
#
# WHY THREE FIRINGS. The bot gets one chance a day at something that cannot be
# done late — a message that shows up tomorrow is not an anniversary message. A
# single blip at 09:00 (Slack having a bad minute, the venue's link flapping,
# MSSQL still starting up) would mean it simply never happened, and the only
# trace would be a line in a log nobody reads.
#
# The extra firings cost nothing and cannot double-post: the bot records who it
# has congratulated, so a run that finds the job already done exits without
# saying a word. If 09:00 worked, 09:30 and 10:30 are no-ops. If it didn't,
# they are the reason somebody still gets their message.
#
# Persistent=true covers the other half of the problem: a box that was powered
# off at 09:00 runs the job as soon as it boots.
#
# WHY THE TIMES ARE OFFSET FROM THE BIRTHDAY BOT'S by default: on a morning
# when both fire, two posts landing in the same second read as one noisy blast.
# A few minutes apart they read as two pieces of news. install.sh asks for the
# time, so change it there rather than here.
#
# TIMEZONE — read this before changing the times.
#
# systemd fires OnCalendar on the SYSTEM timezone (`timedatectl`), which is NOT
# necessarily the app's (`--print-timezone`). Where they differ, a bare 09:10
# means 09:10 on the MACHINE's clock: at a venue running the host on UTC and
# the app on Eastern, that posts before dawn, and nothing says so — the timer
# looks right and the bot looks right.
#
# On systemd 252+ pin the zone onto each line so the time means what it says:
#
#     OnCalendar=*-*-* 09:10:00 America/New_York
#
# That is DST-safe, unlike converting to a fixed UTC offset. install.sh writes
# this form automatically when the two zones differ; the plain form below is
# the shipped default because it parses on every systemd version.
#
# After editing: `systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl restart ceplay-anniversaries.timer`
# then confirm with `systemctl list-timers ceplay-anniversaries`.

[Unit]
Description=CEplay work-anniversary Slack bot — daily message

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 09:10:00
OnCalendar=*-*-* 09:40:00
OnCalendar=*-*-* 10:40:00
Persistent=true
RandomizedDelaySec=0

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
